 slightly retracted black inked posterior margin  1 0cm from the anterior blue inked soft tissue margin and is located 1 0cm posterior to the flattened and irregular nipple  The previous biopsy site is tan white to yellow  focally hemorrhagic  indurated  and contains multiple metal clips  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly fatty  tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  which is grossly unremarkable  At the non designated suture within the possible axillary tail area upon dissection  no palpable lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Previous biopsy site to closest posterior slightly retracted margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of previous biopsy site to nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved fibrous tissue at the medial aspect  Also received in the same container  is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned with no obvious masses or lesions grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm aggregate of irregular to elliptical unremarkable tan white skin  The portions are serially sectioned  and representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMYBREAST  RIGHT   MASTOPEXY , Negative.
