Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Alton Brad Farris III  M D  Reports To  JULIE LISA JONES  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Left breast re excision  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE WITH SUTURE GRANULOMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  ISOLATED FOCUS OF SEVERE ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  ADJACENT TO THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  AND GREATER THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE FINAL MARGIN  ATYPICAL COLUMNAR CELL CHANGE  MULTIFOCAL  WITH CALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE   BREAST  LEFT POSTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  ATYPICAL COLUMNAR CELL CHANGE  MULTIFOCAL  WITH CALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  Note  There are foci of atypical columnar cell change scattered throughout the tissue  without relation to the biopsy cavity  These foci can be considered a form of atypical ductal hyperplasia  The atypia ranges from mild to moderate  with only the isolated focus in the medial margin showing severe atypia  and this latter focus is away from the margin  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  scar  left breast   is white and yellow soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The specimen is an unoriented skin ellipse  2 5cm long excised to a depth of 1 5cm  The deep aspect is inked black  The tissue is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin ellipse tips   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin ellipse body  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast medial margin  short sup