one relevant   Office Notes  None relevant     Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental  universal protocol  Examination of the left breast reveals a 2cm  mobile  firm   nodule subareolar     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  verbal consent was obtained  Ultrasound was used for evaluation of the lesion  and guidance of the needle during the procedure in order to avoid the implant   Ultrasound showed a 1 7cm hypoechoic nodule  4 aspirates were performed using  23 and 25 gauge needles with anesthesia and without complications  2 slides were  stained for immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further  evaluation     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to Dr  Hughes in person at 5  o clock P M      The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation          Electronically Signed Out By  Amy Ly MD on REMOVED_DATE 15 33     Hormone Receptor Quantitation    QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS    Breast  left   cellblock  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Rare tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein   The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2   See note     Note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive  nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows     The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained     Som