Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 3 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  History of R IDC  status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy  lumpectomy  and radiation  Now for bilateral simple mastectomy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  BIOPSY SITE  REMOTE   2  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR IRRADIATION  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FOCAL FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  SKIN  LEFT ADDITIONAL BREAST TISSUE   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SKIN  RIGHT  BREAST ADDITIONAL TISSUE   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  The specimen is received fresh  labeled  right breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 3cm right breast simple mastectomy specimen  which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm tan  wrinkled nipple areolar complex with a centrally located  inverted 0 9cm in diameter nipple  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating axillary tail  The specimen is inked as follows  Posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a lobulated tan yellow fatty cut surfaces with an abundant amount of interspersed dense  nodular gray white fibrous tissue  The latter is predominantly located within the central lower aspect of the specimen  there is a slightly puckered area within the upper outer quadrant that is continuous with the remainder of the fibrous tissue  The puckered area extends to 1 5cm of the posterior resection margin  No other masses or lesions are grossly identified  No lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sec