Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  WACC 2 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  NAOMI R  LEEDS  M D  PHOEBE E FREER  M D  ELIZABETH A RAFFERTY  M D  Resident  Anna McDonald  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results Reason for Addendum  3  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 57 year old woman with a family history of breast cancer  She has a palpable right breast mass which is tender and very suspicious for malignancy on mammography and ultrasound imaging with a BIRADS score of 5  She also has indeterminate coarse heterogeneous microcalcifications in the left breast which are biopsied under a separate requisition  The targeted calcifications are in the specimen  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is positive in the tumor cells  supporting a diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  BREAST  LEFT  CORE BIOPSY  HIGH GRADE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is focally disrupted and a component of invasive ductal carcinoma cannot be excluded  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor and progesterone receptor will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast ultrasound core   are five cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast area core anterior   are multiple cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Also received in the same container is a blue cassette which is opened to reveal three fibrofatty tissue cores measuring from REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm which are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  A large component of the tumor does not stain for progesterone receptor protein  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  69  to chromosome 17 signals  94  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  3 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  3 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  report_end  , Positive.
