 consistent with fat necrosis  The cavity comes to 3 0cm of the posterior margin and 2 8cm of the anterior margin  and is located in the probable lower outer quadrant  No other gross abnormalities are identified  Sectioning of the probable upper outer quadrant reveals several tan pink nodules up to 2 0cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity submitted from apparent medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node each cassette  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY WITH AXILLARY SAMPLING  report_end  , Positive.
