obulated adipose tissue with focal areas of scant tan white rubbery  focally nodular  fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative mass in relation to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative mass in relation to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative skin at site of puckering   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative away  upper outer quadrant  at 10 o clock position   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative uninvolved  lower outer quadrant  at 7 o clock position   Received fresh  labeled  right breast final inferior deep margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of yellow red fibroadipose tissue  received with 2 sutures denoting the final margin  The stitched aspect is inked in black  specimen is serially sectioned and representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right mastectomy flap   are 2 irregular portions of wrinkled white skin  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  No masses or lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday August 04   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 11 59PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Right  Final Inferior Deep Margin   Excision PART C  Skin  Right Mastectomy Flap   Excision  report_end  , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 25 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  