kin surface at the periphery of the areola displays several tan pink slightly raised flat tan red lesions ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Also noted in the upper outer quadrant of the skin are several additional raised flat tan lesions up to 0 7cm in greatest dimension  which come to 0 2cm of the skin margin  There are 2 hemorrhagic umbilicated semicircular scars along the medial aspect of the areola  which measure REMOVED_DATE and 2 4cm  The scars come to 1 8cm of the closest medial skin margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm stellate gray white scar surrounded by silver metal clips  which comes to 0 6cm of the posterior margin and which abuts the skin  The remaining cut surface displays diffuse dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals no definitive lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin lesions   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire scar with posterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue immediately lateral to scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative uninvolved mammary tissue from upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper outer quadrant  which may represent lymph nodes  Also received in the specimen container is an REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm portion of tan pink skin  excised to a depth of 1 8cm  The skin surface displays several raised flat tan lesions ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  0 1cm  The lesions come to 0 3cm of the skin margin  Representative sections including the skin lesions are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LYMPH NODE  LEFT BREAST SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MAL