Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Evan Farkash  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Right mastectomy for focal invasive ductal carcinoma and multifocal invasive lobular carcinoma  with REMOVED_DATE positive lymph nodes  status post excision with positive margins  Status post chemotherapy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   0 2 CM FROM MARGINS  2  EXTENSIVE LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   3  FOCAL FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  5  RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN    right mastectomy   is a mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 7cm  which is surfaced by a 20 x 10 8cm ellipse of skin  containing a nipple measuring 1 4cm in greatest diameter that is elevated 1 1cm above the surrounding areola  The nipple is soft and unremarkable  The ellipse is notable for a 6 cm scar  well healed  located 2cm from the nipple  The specimen has been oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect of the specimen  The anterior aspect of the specimen is inked blue  the posterior is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a stellate shaped region  located directly below the skin scar in the lower inner quadrant  The stellate shaped region  consistent with prior biopsy site  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and is located 0 9cm from the posterior margin and 3cm below the skin ellipse  There is a large  well circumscribed region of firm fibrous tissue measuring 6 0cm in greatest dimension  which is lateral to the stellate shaped region  Scattered throughout the lower inner quadrant are several small  tan  fibrotic  irregular nodular areas  The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Stellate mass from lateral to medial  with mass to posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Well circumscribed  large lobulated areas of fibrosis   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant nodular areas   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sediment in the fixative    blood   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 16   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 23 42PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Positive.
