Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 54 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   Tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 93 at 13 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin are four soft  tan yellow to tan pink cores of tissue  ranging from 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  submitted entirely in A  Gross Description by  John Allick Resident  Andrea Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Radiology Outpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  STEPHANIE L  SHAPIRO  M D  PHOEBE E FREER  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 30 year old woman with epidermal nevus syndrome and right bloody nipple discharge  An MRI at a referring hospital demonstrated an enhancing mass in the right breast  An ultrasound exam demonstrated 2 hypoechoic masses  Mass A is at 9 00 o clock  Mass B is at 3 00 o clock  both are 3cm from nipple  The differential diagnosis for mass A is hamartoma versus fibroadenoma  The differential diagnosis for mass B is a cyst versus fibroadenoma versus hamartoma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  RIGHT  9 00   CORE BIOPSY 1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE 2  COMPLEX SCLEROSING INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  SEE NOTE  B  BREAST  RIGHT  3 00   CORE BIOPSY FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH CYST WALL  NOTE  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern highlights the absence of a myoepithelial layer in areas of invasive ductal carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  